1
00:00:06,132 --> 00:00:07,633
<i>Ben, Regina is here.</i>

2
00:00:07,717 --> 00:00:09,844
<i>- Can you make it?</i>
- <i>All right, I'll try to find a way.</i>

3
00:00:11,679 --> 00:00:13,556
<i>Papa loves me! They love me!</i>

4
00:00:20,146 --> 00:00:22,690
Did you kill Joel too? Tell me!

5
00:00:23,065 --> 00:00:24,066
Speak up!

6
00:00:25,568 --> 00:00:26,986
<i>Tell me the truth.</i>

7
00:00:27,570 --> 00:00:28,612
<i>Or else...</i>

8
00:00:28,696 --> 00:00:30,322
<i>I'll tell everyone about your secret.</i>

9
00:00:32,074 --> 00:00:34,076
<i>They will find out who you really are.</i>

10
00:00:35,536 --> 00:00:37,037
You're a murderer!

11
00:00:39,832 --> 00:00:42,334
Why do you keep

12
00:00:42,418 --> 00:00:44,253
hiding things from me?

13
00:01:02,104 --> 00:01:03,272
Regina.

14
00:01:05,566 --> 00:01:07,067
There you are.

15
00:01:07,735 --> 00:01:08,986
Is it time?

16
00:01:11,947 --> 00:01:13,365
Do I still need those?

17
00:01:14,116 --> 00:01:15,326
I'm fine.

18
00:01:18,287 --> 00:01:19,330
Them.

19
00:01:19,413 --> 00:01:21,165
They're the ones who need the medicine.

20
00:01:21,957 --> 00:01:25,127
But these will help keep you more stable.

21
00:01:27,046 --> 00:01:28,130
Here.

22
00:01:47,817 --> 00:01:51,320
But Mara, do you really think I'm okay?

23
00:01:59,036 --> 00:02:01,038
I want to get out of here.

24
00:02:02,039 --> 00:02:04,041
Joel's waiting for me.

25
00:02:06,961 --> 00:02:11,298
You know, only the doctors can say

26
00:02:11,382 --> 00:02:13,843
whether you're ready to leave or not.

27
00:02:16,428 --> 00:02:18,264
Maybe you could ask them?

28
00:02:23,185 --> 00:02:25,521
Sure. I'll ask them for you, okay?

29
00:02:27,481 --> 00:02:31,151
And I was hoping you'd stay here with me.

30
00:02:32,444 --> 00:02:34,029
You're my only friend.

31
00:02:35,030 --> 00:02:36,866
Of course I'll stay with you.

32
00:02:59,388 --> 00:03:00,472
Ana?

33
00:03:03,058 --> 00:03:04,143
Ana?

34
00:03:06,687 --> 00:03:07,855
Ana?

35
00:03:09,189 --> 00:03:10,274
Ana...

36
00:03:11,692 --> 00:03:12,776
Ana.

37
00:03:15,946 --> 00:03:17,031
Ana.

38
00:03:17,615 --> 00:03:18,699
Hey.

39
00:03:19,950 --> 00:03:21,619
Hey, it's me.

40
00:03:22,369 --> 00:03:24,538
Ana.

41
00:04:14,004 --> 00:04:15,339
Thank you.

42
00:04:23,055 --> 00:04:25,474
I don't know what I'd do
without you, Mara.

43
00:04:29,937 --> 00:04:31,689
Regina's my friend too.

44
00:04:32,982 --> 00:04:34,984
I'm doing this for her as well.

45
00:04:41,365 --> 00:04:43,283
I've been thinking about
moving her to another facility

46
00:04:43,367 --> 00:04:44,785
where she can get better care.

47
00:04:49,832 --> 00:04:52,584
Ben, your sister's going
to keep running away.

48
00:04:53,877 --> 00:04:56,380
I'm just worried
it'll be harder for us because...

49
00:04:56,463 --> 00:04:58,382
we have no idea where she'll go.

50
00:05:01,135 --> 00:05:03,303
Good thing she needed money.

51
00:05:04,096 --> 00:05:06,765
She wanted to sell a painting,
so she came back.

52
00:05:12,604 --> 00:05:14,606
What if I move you to another apartment?

53
00:05:16,608 --> 00:05:17,860
Why?

54
00:05:20,154 --> 00:05:22,489
Shouldn't we stay close to you?

55
00:05:25,200 --> 00:05:28,203
Besides, she thinks...

56
00:05:28,746 --> 00:05:32,499
Joel will come back here for her,
so she'll keep coming back too.

57
00:05:35,627 --> 00:05:37,880
I hope that monster never does.

58
00:05:42,509 --> 00:05:45,012
He'll only ruin my sister's life again.

59
00:05:46,847 --> 00:05:49,433
That Joel really is a jerk.

60
00:05:51,518 --> 00:05:53,771
But your sister loves him so much.

61
00:05:55,481 --> 00:05:57,483
No matter how long it takes,

62
00:05:58,275 --> 00:06:00,360
Regina will keep waiting for him.

63
00:06:03,072 --> 00:06:05,824
How many hours
has he been ignoring your calls?

64
00:06:06,992 --> 00:06:09,495
I've been calling him
since this morning.

65
00:06:11,622 --> 00:06:13,791

Well, he is a busy man, Ana.

66
00:06:13,874 --> 00:06:16,502
And you know where he was going,
he told you.

67
00:06:16,585 --> 00:06:18,003
And you let him.

68
00:06:18,962 --> 00:06:22,049

Yeah, but I really have a bad feeling.

69
00:06:23,467 --> 00:06:25,135
I don't want to be suspicious.

70
00:06:25,219 --> 00:06:26,970
God knows I don't.

71
00:06:28,764 --> 00:06:31,266
But every time we're apart,

72
00:06:31,725 --> 00:06:35,312
I can't help but think
he's with someone else.

73
00:06:35,395 --> 00:06:38,565
Ana, don't let your mind run wild.

74
00:06:39,691 --> 00:06:40,609
No.

75
00:06:40,692 --> 00:06:43,487
I need to know where he is,
what he's doing,

76
00:06:43,570 --> 00:06:45,322
and who he's with.

77
00:06:46,365 --> 00:06:48,367
Do you really need
to know everything, Ana?

78
00:06:48,450 --> 00:06:50,369
- As in?
- I'm his wife!

79
00:06:51,995 --> 00:06:54,832
If I don't know everything,
then what does that make me?

80
00:06:57,126 --> 00:07:00,462
Maybe Eric really did take Angel.

81
00:07:00,838 --> 00:07:03,590
<i>Bridge already said</i>
<i>that jerk doesn't know anything.</i>

82
00:07:03,674 --> 00:07:05,342
<i>But what if he was lying?</i>

83
00:07:05,425 --> 00:07:07,177
I talked to him myself.

84
00:07:07,261 --> 00:07:08,762
I saw it. I could tell.

85
00:07:08,846 --> 00:07:11,598
I know he doesn't know where Angel is.

86
00:07:12,266 --> 00:07:14,017
That poor girl.

87
00:07:14,101 --> 00:07:15,978
She'd been getting beaten over and over.

88
00:07:16,061 --> 00:07:17,896
Why didn't she just leave?

89
00:07:17,980 --> 00:07:19,314
Because she loved Eric!

90
00:07:19,398 --> 00:07:21,024
<i>That's why she was foolish.</i>

91
00:07:21,108 --> 00:07:22,693
<i>Screw that kind of love.</i>

92
00:07:22,776 --> 00:07:24,903
<i>That's why when I fall in love,</i>
<i>I keep it balanced.</i>

93
00:07:24,987 --> 00:07:28,407
<i>I don't give it everything. Maybe 63%.</i>

94
00:07:29,283 --> 00:07:32,786
But Angel gave 100%.

95
00:07:33,328 --> 00:07:36,582
That's what love does.
It really drives you crazy.

96
00:07:36,999 --> 00:07:39,751
Once you're in love,
your brain stops working.

97
00:07:39,835 --> 00:07:43,422
You'll do things
you never thought you could.

98
00:07:43,505 --> 00:07:46,258
<i>Like they say,</i>
<i>when you're in love,</i>

99
00:07:46,341 --> 00:07:51,430
<i>you become desperate, reckless,</i>
<i>and impossible to stop.</i>

100
00:07:51,513 --> 00:07:55,851
- Exactly.
- Wow. And who are "they"?

101
00:07:55,934 --> 00:07:59,521
Maybe we should ask them
where Angel's hiding.

102
00:08:02,357 --> 00:08:03,692
<i>You're impossible!</i>

103
00:08:04,193 --> 00:08:06,361
<i>Idiot! I'm serious!</i>

104
00:08:10,073 --> 00:08:11,658
Thank you so much.

105
00:08:12,326 --> 00:08:14,995
You've been thanking me nonstop.

106
00:08:16,997 --> 00:08:19,082
You pay my salary, remember?

107
00:08:19,166 --> 00:08:21,293


108
00:08:22,085 --> 00:08:24,004
And honestly,

109
00:08:24,504 --> 00:08:26,590
you've helped my family so many times

110
00:08:26,673 --> 00:08:28,592
when we were the ones in need.

111
00:08:28,675 --> 00:08:30,093
Even so, Mara.

112
00:08:31,136 --> 00:08:34,139
Kindness isn't something you can repay.

113
00:08:35,807 --> 00:08:37,226
Thank you.

114
00:08:38,310 --> 00:08:39,895
We're family now.

115
00:08:42,314 --> 00:08:45,901
So no matter what happens,
I'll always be on your side.

116
00:08:46,777 --> 00:08:48,028
Don't worry.

117
00:08:48,403 --> 00:08:51,490
I'll find a way to visit more often.

118
00:08:55,702 --> 00:08:57,788
You really love your sister, don't you?

119
00:08:59,581 --> 00:09:01,583
I love my sister so much.

120
00:09:03,543 --> 00:09:06,046
There's nothing I want more than...

121
00:09:06,129 --> 00:09:07,881
for her to get better.

122
00:09:10,008 --> 00:09:11,843
I just want her to be okay.

123
00:09:15,222 --> 00:09:17,224
So even though it's been hard...

124
00:09:19,685 --> 00:09:22,604
even when she's said hurtful things...

125
00:09:24,982 --> 00:09:27,484
things brought on by her hallucinations...

126
00:09:32,572 --> 00:09:34,992
things that aren't even real...

127
00:09:36,743 --> 00:09:38,745
you've always been patient with her.

128
00:09:42,749 --> 00:09:46,753
But deep down,
you know you can't tell your wife.

129
00:10:20,954 --> 00:10:22,289
Then again...

130
00:10:22,914 --> 00:10:24,583
I guess you're right.

131
00:10:26,335 --> 00:10:28,503
Why would you tell Ana?

132
00:10:30,339 --> 00:10:32,674
When the two of you met,

133
00:10:33,633 --> 00:10:36,219
you hadn't seen Regina for a long time.

134
00:10:40,223 --> 00:10:42,059
Seventeen years.

135
00:10:44,061 --> 00:10:45,562
Seventeen years.

136
00:10:48,607 --> 00:10:50,525
I thought she was gone.

137
00:10:51,985 --> 00:10:53,987
Who would've thought...

138
00:10:54,905 --> 00:10:57,741
that you'd see Regina again two years ago?

139
00:11:23,392 --> 00:11:25,143
Sir, you might like this.

140
00:11:25,227 --> 00:11:27,062
It's cheap, sir. It's really nice.

141
00:11:27,646 --> 00:11:30,565
Here, hold it. You'll see how good it is.

142
00:11:31,066 --> 00:11:32,401
Look at this one too, sir.

143
00:11:32,484 --> 00:11:34,152
Buy one so I can finally go home.

144
00:11:34,236 --> 00:11:35,570
Help me sell everything, sir.

145
00:11:35,654 --> 00:11:36,988
Here's another one. You might like this.

146
00:11:37,072 --> 00:11:38,240
Ruin?

147
00:11:39,282 --> 00:11:43,036
That's my girlfriend.
That's the nickname she uses.

148
00:11:43,578 --> 00:11:46,665
Since you asked,
my girlfriend's name is Regina Santos.

149
00:11:46,748 --> 00:11:48,750
She's beautiful, but don't hit on her.

150
00:11:49,209 --> 00:11:52,295
Come on, sir. Buy them already.
Take everything.

151
00:11:53,004 --> 00:11:54,339
Is that all you want?

152
00:11:55,715 --> 00:11:58,885
- So I can finally go home.
- <i>But Joel was completely insane.</i>

153
00:11:58,969 --> 00:12:01,388
<i>He only made Regina's life and mind</i>
<i>even more messed up.</i>

154
00:12:01,471 --> 00:12:02,472
My girlfriend's beautiful.

155
00:12:03,723 --> 00:12:06,309
Once Gingging gets better,

156
00:12:10,480 --> 00:12:12,482
I'll tell Ana everything.

157
00:12:18,029 --> 00:12:21,116
So we'll take Regina
to the doctor tomorrow, okay?

158
00:12:23,034 --> 00:12:26,037
I'm impressed with the life
you have built with Ana.

159
00:12:27,289 --> 00:12:29,875
If I were in your situation,

160
00:12:30,584 --> 00:12:33,003
I wouldn't let it be ruined either.

161
00:13:03,033 --> 00:13:04,284
Shit.

162
00:13:08,997 --> 00:13:10,165
Shit!

163
00:13:13,710 --> 00:13:16,463


164
00:13:22,802 --> 00:13:23,887
<i>Ana?</i>

165
00:13:25,263 --> 00:13:27,682

Why aren't you replying to my messages?

166
00:13:27,766 --> 00:13:29,226
You're not answering my calls!

167
00:13:29,309 --> 00:13:31,228

<i>I've been calling you and texting you,</i>

168
00:13:31,311 --> 00:13:32,646
<i>and yet, nothing!</i>

169
00:13:32,729 --> 00:13:35,649
<i>Is it too much to ask for a single reply?</i>

170
00:13:35,732 --> 00:13:37,567
I've been waiting all day!

171
00:13:37,651 --> 00:13:41,488
I've been worried about where you are
and if you're okay!

172
00:13:42,239 --> 00:13:44,824
Have some consideration, Ben!

173
00:13:44,908 --> 00:13:46,034
I'm your wife!

174
00:13:48,328 --> 00:13:49,496
<i>Hello?</i>

175
00:13:50,038 --> 00:13:52,958
What?
Are you not even going to say anything?

176
00:13:53,041 --> 00:13:54,459
Answer me!

177
00:13:54,960 --> 00:13:56,545
Ana? Ana.

178
00:13:57,754 --> 00:13:59,172
Everything is okay.

179
00:13:59,548 --> 00:14:01,049
I just did a lot of work here.

180
00:14:01,132 --> 00:14:03,134
And I left my phone in the car.

181
00:14:03,593 --> 00:14:04,761
Sorry. I'm sorry.

182
00:14:04,844 --> 00:14:07,722
It's my fault that I didn't call you.
I'm really, really sorry.

183
00:14:10,100 --> 00:14:13,353
Make this a video call.
I want to know where you are.

184
00:14:13,979 --> 00:14:15,063
Yeah, okay.

185
00:14:15,146 --> 00:14:16,773
But my phone
might suddenly turn off, okay?

186
00:14:16,856 --> 00:14:17,774
My battery's low.

187
00:14:17,857 --> 00:14:20,735
I want to know where you are!
I want to see you!

188
00:14:20,819 --> 00:14:24,155
Yes, but I can't turn on my camera

189
00:14:24,239 --> 00:14:25,490
because my phone will turn off.

190
00:14:25,574 --> 00:14:28,451
My phone's battery is low.

191
00:14:28,535 --> 00:14:29,869
Then charge it!

192
00:14:31,705 --> 00:14:33,373
I don't have my charger.

193
00:14:36,084 --> 00:14:37,669
How convenient.

194
00:14:39,713 --> 00:14:42,048
You always have an excuse.

195
00:14:42,966 --> 00:14:44,384
Low battery.

196
00:14:44,884 --> 00:14:46,386
<i>Your charger's not working.</i>

197
00:14:46,928 --> 00:14:48,513
<i>Bad signal.</i>

198
00:14:48,930 --> 00:14:50,348
Okay. Ana.

199
00:14:50,890 --> 00:14:51,891
Ana?

200
00:14:52,517 --> 00:14:55,020
Okay, please listen,
I understand this is frustrating,

201
00:14:55,103 --> 00:14:57,439
and I'm sorry for making you worry.

202
00:14:59,316 --> 00:15:01,234
<i>But you have to trust me, okay?</i>

203
00:15:02,402 --> 00:15:03,653
This is my fault.

204
00:15:04,362 --> 00:15:05,530
I'm sorry.

205
00:15:05,947 --> 00:15:08,366
I'm very sorry. It won't happen again.

206
00:15:10,660 --> 00:15:11,828
<i>Hello?</i>

207
00:15:11,911 --> 00:15:13,163
Hello?

208
00:15:15,206 --> 00:15:16,374
Okay.

209
00:15:19,461 --> 00:15:21,796
Do you want me
to come home to you right now?

210
00:15:23,673 --> 00:15:25,592
I can go home now, okay?

211
00:15:25,675 --> 00:15:27,427
I'll be there by morning.

212
00:15:27,510 --> 00:15:29,095
<i>I can go home to you.</i>

213
00:15:29,512 --> 00:15:30,930
<i>Do you want that?</i>

214
00:15:32,390 --> 00:15:33,558
No.

215
00:15:35,018 --> 00:15:37,270
Your meeting's important, right?

216
00:15:38,980 --> 00:15:41,483
I just want to know where you are.

217
00:15:45,695 --> 00:15:48,865
Is it too much to ask you
to update your wife?

218
00:15:51,493 --> 00:15:53,495
<i>Yes. I understand.</i>

219
00:15:54,746 --> 00:15:55,830
I understand.

220
00:15:57,374 --> 00:15:58,792
This won't happen again.

221
00:16:00,126 --> 00:16:01,461
I'm sorry.

222
00:16:04,047 --> 00:16:05,548
I need to rest.

223
00:16:09,844 --> 00:16:10,929
Okay.

224
00:16:12,472 --> 00:16:14,724
I'm sorry again. I love you, stranger.

225
00:16:57,058 --> 00:16:58,226
Okay?

226
00:16:59,227 --> 00:17:00,478
Are you all right?

227
00:17:06,234 --> 00:17:07,485
I'll update you.

228
00:17:41,227 --> 00:17:43,438
<i>Call me when you're not busy anymore.</i>

229
00:17:44,147 --> 00:17:46,983
<i>I'm sorry again. I love you.</i>

230
00:18:17,931 --> 00:18:19,849
Mara, we're done.

231
00:18:25,563 --> 00:18:28,483
She doesn't have maintenance medication
after discharge?

232
00:18:29,025 --> 00:18:31,444
She did, but she stopped taking it.

233
00:18:32,445 --> 00:18:35,198
She suddenly disappeared
because she ran away.

234
00:18:35,281 --> 00:18:38,076
At the moment,
based on what you're saying,

235
00:18:38,159 --> 00:18:40,537
it sounds like a recurrence of psychosis.

236
00:18:43,873 --> 00:18:45,375
Doc, to be honest,

237
00:18:45,458 --> 00:18:48,545
we're also having a hard time
talking to her,

238
00:18:48,628 --> 00:18:51,548
especially when she's having an episode.

239
00:18:52,173 --> 00:18:55,760
Mara,
you, of all people, should know this.

240
00:18:55,844 --> 00:18:59,389
We don't confront her delusion directly.

241
00:18:59,472 --> 00:19:01,474
She's not grounded in reality
during that time.

242
00:19:01,558 --> 00:19:03,476
So arguing won't help.

243
00:19:03,560 --> 00:19:07,397
Instead, acknowledge the emotion,
not the content.

244
00:20:00,283 --> 00:20:02,785
We will restart antipsychotic medication.

245
00:20:03,912 --> 00:20:05,747
We'll start with a low dose for now.

246
00:20:05,830 --> 00:20:10,835
And then, we'll adjust
depending on Regina's response to it.

247
00:20:10,919 --> 00:20:12,086
Okay, Doc.

248
00:20:15,882 --> 00:20:18,176
Pick up, pick up. Pick up.

249
00:20:22,972 --> 00:20:25,558
Consistent follow-up
is the key, Mara.

250
00:20:26,059 --> 00:20:29,062
Noted, Doc.

251
00:20:29,145 --> 00:20:30,772
Thank you.

252
00:20:30,855 --> 00:20:33,858
I also hope that on our next appointment,

253
00:20:33,942 --> 00:20:36,152
we can be with her brother.

254
00:20:36,235 --> 00:20:38,237
She always talks about him.

255
00:20:38,321 --> 00:20:40,448
Do you know where he is?

256
00:20:42,200 --> 00:20:43,618
Um...

257
00:20:44,744 --> 00:20:47,246
I'm sorry. I don't know where he is.

258
00:20:47,330 --> 00:20:49,248
He hasn't contacted us yet.

259
00:20:55,129 --> 00:20:58,800
Ms. Ana, your mother's here.

260
00:20:58,883 --> 00:21:00,051
Excuse me.

261
00:21:00,718 --> 00:21:02,220
- Hi, dear.
- Mom.

262
00:21:05,848 --> 00:21:07,100
Oh?

263
00:21:07,183 --> 00:21:09,268
Why are you just standing there?

264
00:21:09,352 --> 00:21:10,770
Go wait for me outside!

265
00:21:10,853 --> 00:21:12,355
Go on! Get out!

266
00:21:13,231 --> 00:21:15,566
Why did he also come in?

267
00:21:15,650 --> 00:21:17,068
Dear...

268
00:21:23,408 --> 00:21:25,243
<i>Yes, we'll proceed.</i>

269
00:21:25,326 --> 00:21:29,163
<i>Beth, my friend wants to hire you</i>
<i>for her father-in-law.</i>

270
00:21:30,623 --> 00:21:32,792
Sure, I can do that.

271
00:21:33,418 --> 00:21:36,671
<i>But she's asking if you have a permit.</i>

272
00:21:36,754 --> 00:21:39,340
<i>She's wondering</i>
<i>if you're a real physical therapist.</i>

273
00:21:40,299 --> 00:21:43,428
Yes, I'm a licensed PT, ma'am.

274
00:21:43,511 --> 00:21:46,264
But I'll also ask around
for what other permits I need

275
00:21:46,347 --> 00:21:49,267
to practice privately here in Vallente.

276
00:21:50,476 --> 00:21:52,478
<i>Do that first, okay?</i>

277
00:21:52,562 --> 00:21:55,565
<i>When that's all ready,</i>
<i>you can call my friend then.</i>

278
00:21:56,441 --> 00:21:58,526
Okay, ma'am. Thank you.

279
00:22:08,786 --> 00:22:11,956
<i>Beth, I added Attorney.</i>
<i>I'm now friends with my idol!</i>

280
00:22:15,334 --> 00:22:18,838
<i>You're so embarrassing.</i>

281
00:22:29,766 --> 00:22:32,268
<i>Attorney, how's it going?</i>

282
00:22:48,367 --> 00:22:51,704
<i>I'm sorry if Harry bothered you.</i>

283
00:23:02,548 --> 00:23:03,800
<i>It's fine.</i>

284
00:23:14,644 --> 00:23:16,562
<i>He just looks up to you a lot.</i>

285
00:23:26,239 --> 00:23:27,406
<i>Attorney...</i>

286
00:23:27,949 --> 00:23:29,283
<i>can I call you?</i>

287
00:23:31,953 --> 00:23:33,704
<i>Sure.</i>

288
00:23:39,043 --> 00:23:41,045
- <i>Hello, Beth.</i>
- Attorney!

289
00:23:41,963 --> 00:23:45,800
Um, I'm sorry if I'm disturbing you.

290
00:23:45,883 --> 00:23:47,468
No, it's okay.

291
00:23:47,969 --> 00:23:49,971
What can I do for you?

292
00:23:50,054 --> 00:23:52,557
<i>Attorney, it's nothing.</i>
<i>I just wanted to say hi.</i>

293
00:23:54,642 --> 00:23:57,061
Why did you even bring him with you?

294
00:23:57,770 --> 00:24:00,857
I wanted him to see your atelier.

295
00:24:02,233 --> 00:24:03,568
What for?

296
00:24:04,610 --> 00:24:08,447
So that he can see
what he chose to walk away from.

297
00:24:08,531 --> 00:24:10,575
And how far you've come...

298
00:24:10,658 --> 00:24:12,326
even if he left.

299
00:24:14,328 --> 00:24:17,415
Mom,
I don't need his validation.

300
00:24:18,416 --> 00:24:20,042
So what's your problem?

301
00:24:20,960 --> 00:24:22,628
What are you talking about?

302
00:24:24,338 --> 00:24:25,506
Ana...

303
00:24:26,465 --> 00:24:28,551
News travels fast.

304
00:24:29,343 --> 00:24:31,012
Virgie has a cell phone.

305
00:24:31,637 --> 00:24:34,056
They say
you were going mad here yesterday.

306
00:24:35,850 --> 00:24:37,518
I'm just stressed.

307
00:24:38,227 --> 00:24:39,478
Is it Ben?

308
00:24:48,321 --> 00:24:51,282
<i>How's your shoulder?</i>
<i>Does it still hurt?</i>

309
00:24:51,365 --> 00:24:52,491
Uh...

310
00:24:52,575 --> 00:24:54,577
No, it's okay. Thank you.

311
00:24:55,244 --> 00:24:56,579
How can I help you, Beth?

312
00:24:59,207 --> 00:25:00,458
Um...

313
00:25:00,541 --> 00:25:03,085
Well, I have a bit of a problem.

314
00:25:05,338 --> 00:25:08,507
The mother of one of my patients

315
00:25:09,050 --> 00:25:11,969
is referring a potential client to me.

316
00:25:13,304 --> 00:25:18,559
Do you know what permits I need
before I can practice again, Attorney?

317
00:25:18,643 --> 00:25:19,894
<i>Uh...</i>

318
00:25:19,977 --> 00:25:21,395
<i>I'm not sure about the exact steps,</i>

319
00:25:21,479 --> 00:25:26,150
<i>but basically, you just need to go there</i>

320
00:25:26,234 --> 00:25:28,694
<i>and register Vallente</i>

321
00:25:28,778 --> 00:25:31,530
<i>as the location of your private practice.</i>

322
00:25:32,114 --> 00:25:33,449
Ah...

323
00:25:34,867 --> 00:25:37,286
- That's it?
<i>- Yes.</i>

324
00:25:37,370 --> 00:25:41,207
You can verify it
at the information office.

325
00:25:41,707 --> 00:25:43,209
Just bring your license.

326
00:25:44,377 --> 00:25:46,462
<i>Is there anything else</i>
<i>I can do for you, Beth?</i>

327
00:25:47,171 --> 00:25:48,589
Oh, wait, Attorney.

328
00:25:48,673 --> 00:25:50,758
Will I be seeing you later?

329
00:25:50,841 --> 00:25:53,094
We have a session today, remember?

330
00:25:55,554 --> 00:25:58,474
Oh, okay, Beth,
I'm really sorry, but...

331
00:25:59,308 --> 00:26:00,893
we'll have to reschedule.

332
00:26:00,977 --> 00:26:02,186
I'm busy today.

333
00:26:02,728 --> 00:26:04,480
Ah, all right, Attorney.

334
00:26:05,064 --> 00:26:06,399
Take care.

335
00:26:06,482 --> 00:26:08,734
<i>Okay, Beth.</i>
<i>You too. Thank you.</i>

336
00:26:16,492 --> 00:26:17,994
Ben's out of town, Mom.

337
00:26:18,077 --> 00:26:20,663
He's dealing
with something at the <i>azucarera.</i>

338
00:26:21,205 --> 00:26:25,459
I don't care
what your husband is doing or where he is.

339
00:26:25,543 --> 00:26:27,211
What I'm asking is...

340
00:26:27,753 --> 00:26:29,588
is Ben the problem?

341
00:26:31,257 --> 00:26:34,343
Uh, Joonjin,
can you please leave us first?

342
00:26:43,519 --> 00:26:44,770
Is he having an affair?

343
00:26:49,734 --> 00:26:51,152
Ma!

344
00:26:51,235 --> 00:26:52,153
What?

345
00:26:52,236 --> 00:26:54,196
That is outrageous!

346
00:26:55,531 --> 00:26:58,326
I'll admit, Ana,
I didn't like him at first.

347
00:26:58,409 --> 00:26:59,744
But...

348
00:26:59,827 --> 00:27:01,203
he stayed.

349
00:27:01,287 --> 00:27:02,705
Showed up.

350
00:27:02,788 --> 00:27:04,498
He took care of you.

351
00:27:04,582 --> 00:27:07,335
He has been working so hard.

352
00:27:07,418 --> 00:27:11,005
And now, he's one of the most
respected lawyers in town.

353
00:27:11,088 --> 00:27:13,382
Where is this going, Ma?

354
00:27:13,466 --> 00:27:18,137
He fits into your life now.

355
00:27:18,220 --> 00:27:19,555
Into your world.

356
00:27:20,389 --> 00:27:22,308
But in this world of yours, Ana,

357
00:27:23,184 --> 00:27:26,771
there are plenty of women
who want your husband.

358
00:27:27,938 --> 00:27:32,943
He's handsome, kind, smart, rich--

359
00:27:33,027 --> 00:27:34,612
So do I just do nothing?

360
00:27:34,695 --> 00:27:37,114
Of course not!

361
00:27:37,198 --> 00:27:38,824
All I'm saying is,

362
00:27:39,367 --> 00:27:42,453
protect your marriage
by keeping an eye on your husband.

363
00:27:44,538 --> 00:27:46,624
Ma, Ben and I are okay.

364
00:27:46,707 --> 00:27:49,043
He's just out of town for a work trip.

365
00:27:49,668 --> 00:27:51,337
But we're okay.

366
00:27:52,797 --> 00:27:55,174
- Okay.
- Yeah.

367
00:27:55,257 --> 00:27:56,425
All right.

368
00:27:59,637 --> 00:28:01,639
I have to go, all right?

369
00:28:01,722 --> 00:28:03,474
- Okay.
- Take care.

370
00:28:15,361 --> 00:28:16,946
It's beautiful, Ging.

371
00:28:18,906 --> 00:28:20,366
So beautiful.

372
00:28:23,744 --> 00:28:25,913
To me, you're the best.

373
00:28:26,539 --> 00:28:27,790
The best.

374
00:28:33,045 --> 00:28:34,130
All right.

375
00:28:35,840 --> 00:28:38,843
If you need anything,
let Mara know.

376
00:28:38,926 --> 00:28:40,344
I'll get it for you.

377
00:28:41,595 --> 00:28:42,763
Okay.

378
00:28:45,599 --> 00:28:46,851
Be a good girl.

379
00:28:47,393 --> 00:28:48,477
I am.

380
00:28:49,019 --> 00:28:50,438
Keep it that way.

381
00:28:51,313 --> 00:28:52,481
Okay.

382
00:28:56,026 --> 00:28:57,111
Ging.

383
00:28:58,320 --> 00:28:59,738
Don't forget, okay?

384
00:29:01,282 --> 00:29:03,284
It's you and me against the world.

385
00:29:04,243 --> 00:29:05,661
Just the two of us.

386
00:29:07,079 --> 00:29:08,497
I love you.

387
00:29:10,541 --> 00:29:11,876
I want money.

388
00:29:13,335 --> 00:29:16,005
- Huh?
- Tell Mara to sell my paintings.

389
00:29:18,632 --> 00:29:20,384
I will give you money.

390
00:29:20,468 --> 00:29:21,677
I want a lot of it.

391
00:29:21,760 --> 00:29:23,345
A lot of money.

392
00:29:24,180 --> 00:29:26,015
I need to find Joel.

393
00:29:26,807 --> 00:29:28,976
So sell all of my paintings.

394
00:30:04,261 --> 00:30:05,679
Hey, stranger.

395
00:30:17,650 --> 00:30:19,151
This is for you.

396
00:30:21,946 --> 00:30:23,197
I'm sorry.

397
00:30:25,366 --> 00:30:26,867
You look tired.

398
00:30:27,618 --> 00:30:28,869
Let's eat.

399
00:30:31,580 --> 00:30:32,581
Okay.

400
00:30:44,718 --> 00:30:45,970
Are we okay?

401
00:30:48,806 --> 00:30:50,474
Ging?

402
00:30:50,558 --> 00:30:52,059
Time to eat.

403
00:30:52,643 --> 00:30:53,644
Ging...

404
00:30:54,144 --> 00:30:56,355
Ging! Ging!

405
00:30:56,438 --> 00:30:59,942
Ging, what have you done?
What have you done?

406
00:31:00,025 --> 00:31:02,278
Why did you hurt yourself? Ging!

407
00:31:02,361 --> 00:31:03,862
Ging, wake up! Ging!

408
00:31:03,946 --> 00:31:06,073
Please wake up! Oh, God!

409
00:31:15,249 --> 00:31:16,750
That wasn't funny.

410
00:31:16,834 --> 00:31:19,461
Ging, what the hell?

411
00:31:19,545 --> 00:31:21,463
This is not funny!

412
00:31:35,811 --> 00:31:37,521
Regina, stop! You'll hurt yourself!

413
00:31:37,605 --> 00:31:39,857
Why did you tell Ben Joel was here?

414
00:31:40,524 --> 00:31:42,276
Do you want to hurt me?

415
00:31:42,359 --> 00:31:43,902
You want to hurt me, huh?

416
00:31:44,612 --> 00:31:46,697
Ben, she had an episode again.

417
00:31:48,574 --> 00:31:50,159
Ben, she's getting worse.

418
00:31:50,242 --> 00:31:53,954
I used to be able to calm her down.
Now, only her meds can.

419
00:31:54,038 --> 00:31:55,289
This is not good.

420
00:32:01,587 --> 00:32:02,713
All right, let's meet.

421
00:32:02,796 --> 00:32:05,049
But we have to be quick.
I can't be gone long.

422
00:32:24,234 --> 00:32:25,903
This is so hard.

423
00:32:28,781 --> 00:32:31,033
<i>I can't keep doing this, Ben.</i>

424
00:32:36,372 --> 00:32:38,040
- Mara?
- Hmm?

425
00:32:38,123 --> 00:32:39,875
We're friends, aren't we?

426
00:32:41,418 --> 00:32:42,753
Of course.

427
00:32:44,129 --> 00:32:46,215
Tell me the truth.

428
00:32:47,132 --> 00:32:48,801
What do you really want?

429
00:32:50,928 --> 00:32:52,680
We want the same thing, Ging.

430
00:32:53,931 --> 00:32:55,849
For you to get better.

431
00:33:08,487 --> 00:33:10,155
I'll do that, Nanny.

432
00:33:11,073 --> 00:33:12,408
- Are you sure?
- Yes.

433
00:33:12,491 --> 00:33:15,160
You should get some rest.
I can't sleep anyway.

434
00:33:15,703 --> 00:33:17,830
- Okay then.
- Okay.

435
00:33:17,913 --> 00:33:20,499
- Mm-hmm. Thank you.
- Okay. Good night.

436
00:33:20,582 --> 00:33:21,667
Good night.

437
00:34:23,312 --> 00:34:24,396
Hello?

438
00:34:25,230 --> 00:34:27,733
<i>Attorney, what can I do for you?</i>

439
00:34:28,358 --> 00:34:29,943
Did I catch you at a bad time?

440
00:34:30,360 --> 00:34:34,114
<i>Not at all. Is this about the cellphone?</i>

441
00:34:34,198 --> 00:34:35,282
Yes, Chairman.

442
00:34:35,365 --> 00:34:37,701
Has anyone claimed it?

443
00:34:38,410 --> 00:34:39,745
<i>Not yet.</i>

444
00:34:40,162 --> 00:34:42,664
<i>Ma'am Ana asked about it too.</i>

445
00:34:42,748 --> 00:34:43,791
She did?

446
00:34:43,874 --> 00:34:46,293
<i>Yes. She called me the other night.</i>

447
00:34:46,376 --> 00:34:50,714
<i>Don't worry, if someone claims it,</i>
<i>I'll let you know right away.</i>

448
00:34:51,715 --> 00:34:53,467
Okay, okay.

449
00:34:53,550 --> 00:34:54,760
Okay, please. Thank you, Chairman.

450
00:34:54,843 --> 00:34:56,512
Sorry for calling this late.

451
00:35:10,275 --> 00:35:11,360
Ugh!

452
00:35:11,443 --> 00:35:12,611
Oh, man!

453
00:35:22,329 --> 00:35:23,747
Fuck!

454
00:35:24,331 --> 00:35:28,126
Take it easy, Ana.
You don't want to hurt yourself.

455
00:35:28,210 --> 00:35:30,504
I'm fine.

456
00:35:50,858 --> 00:35:53,026
- There you go.
- Thank you.

457
00:35:59,074 --> 00:36:01,910
Is that Rea Villa?

458
00:36:04,121 --> 00:36:05,539
I think so.

459
00:36:05,622 --> 00:36:07,207
She looks different.

460
00:36:07,666 --> 00:36:10,085
But what's she doing here?
I thought they moved abroad.

461
00:36:10,168 --> 00:36:11,837
You haven't heard?

462
00:36:11,920 --> 00:36:13,589
They have separated.

463
00:36:14,047 --> 00:36:15,632
She and her husband split up?

464
00:36:15,716 --> 00:36:17,384
Apparently, yes.

465
00:36:17,467 --> 00:36:20,137
There was someone else. A third party.

466
00:36:20,220 --> 00:36:22,097
The guy cheated?

467
00:36:22,180 --> 00:36:23,932
I've heard, yeah.

468
00:36:24,016 --> 00:36:25,183
It was messy.

469
00:36:25,267 --> 00:36:27,269
Good thing they don't have kids.

470
00:36:27,769 --> 00:36:30,939
Apparently, the guy had a lot of secrets.

471
00:36:31,732 --> 00:36:34,318
So when the truth came out,
all hell broke loose.

472
00:36:39,615 --> 00:36:40,949
Listen, Carlos.

473
00:36:41,033 --> 00:36:42,951
Don't you ever do that to me.

474
00:36:43,035 --> 00:36:44,912
If you do,
I'll cut your balls off.

475
00:36:44,995 --> 00:36:46,496
That won't be necessary.

476
00:36:46,580 --> 00:36:48,540
I would never do that to you.

477
00:36:48,624 --> 00:36:50,083
You'd better not.

478
00:36:50,167 --> 00:36:52,920
- You swear? Good.
- Never. I swear.

479
00:37:18,028 --> 00:37:19,529
Mara, water, please!

480
00:37:48,684 --> 00:37:49,726
Hello?

481
00:37:52,854 --> 00:37:54,523
<i> Hello? Who is this?</i>

482
00:37:58,610 --> 00:38:00,112
H-Hello?

483
00:38:00,195 --> 00:38:01,863
Who are you?

484
00:38:03,407 --> 00:38:04,825
Do you know Ben--

485
00:38:04,908 --> 00:38:05,993
Benjamin...

486
00:38:06,702 --> 00:38:08,620
<i>Benjamin Santos?</i>

487
00:38:08,704 --> 00:38:09,746
Who is this?

488
00:38:10,872 --> 00:38:12,958
Answer my question!

489
00:38:13,709 --> 00:38:16,878
Do you know Benjamin Santos?

490
00:38:18,588 --> 00:38:19,756
Fuck you!

491
00:38:35,313 --> 00:38:37,816
W-What...

492
00:38:40,485 --> 00:38:42,070
Ignore it.

493
00:38:43,196 --> 00:38:44,364
Why?

494
00:38:44,448 --> 00:38:46,241
I answered it already.
They were looking for Ben.

495
00:38:46,324 --> 00:38:49,119
What? Who was it?

496
00:38:49,202 --> 00:38:51,872
Some woman was asking about Ben.

497
00:38:51,955 --> 00:38:52,956
W-What did she say?

498
00:38:53,040 --> 00:38:55,751
She didn't tell me who she was! Idiot.

499
00:38:56,543 --> 00:38:57,711
What did you say?

500
00:38:57,794 --> 00:39:00,213
Nothing! What if it's a scam?

501
00:39:15,896 --> 00:39:17,147
Uh...

502
00:39:18,690 --> 00:39:20,442
It must be a scammer.

503
00:39:21,943 --> 00:39:24,362
Maybe next time, Ging...

504
00:39:24,446 --> 00:39:26,948
don't answer calls from unknown numbers.

505
00:39:29,868 --> 00:39:31,286
I want water, Mara.

506
00:39:32,871 --> 00:39:34,539
I'm thirsty. Get me water.

507
00:39:45,133 --> 00:39:47,886
<i>You know how persistent she is.</i>

508
00:39:47,969 --> 00:39:49,513
Who did Gingging speak to?

509
00:39:49,596 --> 00:39:52,766
<i>A woman. She didn't give her name.</i>

510
00:39:52,849 --> 00:39:54,351
<i>But she was looking for you.</i>

511
00:39:55,393 --> 00:39:56,812
She was looking for me?

512
00:39:59,064 --> 00:40:00,565
What did they talk about?

513
00:40:02,359 --> 00:40:03,527
<i>She said nothing much.</i>

514
00:40:03,610 --> 00:40:05,862
<i>She dropped the call</i>
<i>when the woman didn't answer.</i>

515
00:40:06,446 --> 00:40:07,781
Okay. Mara.

516
00:40:08,657 --> 00:40:10,075
Destroy your SIM card.

517
00:40:11,409 --> 00:40:12,911
Get a new number.

518
00:40:13,411 --> 00:40:14,913
Then call me right away.

519
00:40:17,332 --> 00:40:18,416
Ben.

520
00:40:21,002 --> 00:40:22,754
Aside from your wife,

521
00:40:23,380 --> 00:40:25,549
are there other people looking for you?

522
00:40:26,925 --> 00:40:29,344
I haven't told anyone about you.

523
00:40:29,970 --> 00:40:31,721
So whoever called you...

524
00:40:32,139 --> 00:40:34,141
make sure they won't reach you again.

525
00:41:21,688 --> 00:41:23,690
You want me to trace this number for you?

526
00:41:23,773 --> 00:41:25,275
Kat!

527
00:41:29,070 --> 00:41:30,280
But yes.

528
00:41:30,363 --> 00:41:32,449
You know someone from telecom, right?

529
00:41:32,908 --> 00:41:34,826
- Yeah, but I mean--
- Kat.

530
00:41:34,910 --> 00:41:38,079
I can't hire a private investigator.

531
00:41:38,538 --> 00:41:42,542
I can't risk people knowing
that I'm investigating someone.

532
00:41:42,626 --> 00:41:44,753
Yes, but my contact from the telecom
will still know

533
00:41:44,836 --> 00:41:47,172
- because it will be traced to your number.
- No.

534
00:41:47,255 --> 00:41:48,882
You'll be the one to ask,

535
00:41:48,965 --> 00:41:51,718
so they won't know
that I'm the one who wants it traced.

536
00:41:51,801 --> 00:41:53,386
Ah, is that how you want it?

537
00:41:53,929 --> 00:41:55,764
Oh, my God...

538
00:42:00,477 --> 00:42:02,896
Be grateful that I'm worried about you.

539
00:42:02,979 --> 00:42:05,065
If Carlos finds out what I'm doing--

540
00:42:05,148 --> 00:42:06,399
Kat...

541
00:42:06,483 --> 00:42:07,776
If he doesn't believe you,

542
00:42:07,859 --> 00:42:10,195
I'll handle it.
I'll talk to him.

543
00:42:10,612 --> 00:42:15,617
Besides, what kind of fiancé
would stop his future wife

544
00:42:15,700 --> 00:42:18,203
from worrying about her best friend?

545
00:42:18,286 --> 00:42:20,705
The best friend card.
Really, Ana?

546
00:42:23,792 --> 00:42:25,961
Please, please. Kat, please.

547
00:42:27,420 --> 00:42:29,089
Fine.

548
00:42:29,673 --> 00:42:31,424
Fine, fine, fine.

549
00:42:33,802 --> 00:42:36,680
You know,
Mike is really a jerk.

550
00:42:36,763 --> 00:42:40,350
Imagine, I can't even
go near my own son at his school.

551
00:42:40,433 --> 00:42:44,020
Well, he's really using
his money and connections.

552
00:42:44,354 --> 00:42:46,439
Don't cause any trouble, you hear me?

553
00:42:46,982 --> 00:42:48,483
<i>What do you mean?</i>

554
00:42:49,317 --> 00:42:53,321
You wouldn't want to have more cases
because of Mike, right?

555
00:42:53,947 --> 00:42:57,951
Beth, I have the right to my son.
Even the law recognizes that.

556
00:42:58,034 --> 00:43:00,120
I already told you.

557
00:43:00,203 --> 00:43:02,998
I'm going to ask the attorney.
He will be able to help you.

558
00:43:03,081 --> 00:43:05,500
<i>- Beth.</i>
- What?

559
00:43:06,001 --> 00:43:09,170
Shouldn't he be blocked
from our lives now?

560
00:43:09,254 --> 00:43:11,047
The loyalty testing is over.

561
00:43:11,798 --> 00:43:15,051
How can I do that?
I still have PT sessions with him.

562
00:43:15,552 --> 00:43:18,972
Beth. Let me just remind you.

563
00:43:19,055 --> 00:43:22,475
We can't be involved with our clients.

564
00:43:23,476 --> 00:43:27,397
So I suggest you start staying away
from Ana and Ben.

565
00:43:28,189 --> 00:43:31,192
They hired you to be a loyalty tester
in their relationship,

566
00:43:31,276 --> 00:43:33,486
not to be their friend.

567
00:43:33,570 --> 00:43:36,072
Okay, fine. I get it.

568
00:43:36,156 --> 00:43:38,366
<i>I'll tell you the same thing you told me.</i>

569
00:43:38,450 --> 00:43:40,577
Don't cause any trouble.

570
00:43:40,660 --> 00:43:42,996
<i>I'm hanging up. You should rest.</i>

571
00:43:53,423 --> 00:43:54,924
Please come in, Attorney!

572
00:43:55,008 --> 00:43:56,885
Thank you.
Thank you, thank you very much.

573
00:43:56,968 --> 00:43:59,804
Ma'am Ana just went out for a bit.

574
00:43:59,888 --> 00:44:03,516
She's with Ms. Katrina.
They went to get some coffee.

575
00:44:04,225 --> 00:44:07,228
Yeah. I should've texted her
before coming here.

576
00:44:08,730 --> 00:44:09,898
Anyway...

577
00:44:10,357 --> 00:44:11,691
Oh, Virgie.

578
00:44:12,359 --> 00:44:13,777
Whose charger is this?

579
00:44:14,361 --> 00:44:16,112
Um, it's Ma'am Ana's.

580
00:44:18,198 --> 00:44:20,033
Ana's charger isn't this type.

581
00:44:20,909 --> 00:44:21,910
Ah!

582
00:44:21,993 --> 00:44:25,497
It's probably for the new phone
that was delivered the other day.

583
00:44:27,916 --> 00:44:29,501
Ana has a new phone?

584
00:44:29,584 --> 00:44:30,710
Uh, yes.

585
00:44:30,794 --> 00:44:32,128
The delivery guy said

586
00:44:32,212 --> 00:44:34,297
that Ma'am Ana should be
the one to receive it

587
00:44:34,381 --> 00:44:35,632
since it's a new phone.

588
00:44:36,049 --> 00:44:37,550
Attorney, I have to go.

589
00:44:37,634 --> 00:44:39,386
I have to take a client's measurements.

590
00:44:39,469 --> 00:44:41,721
- Okay, Virgie. Thank you.
- Okay, sir.

591
00:45:08,039 --> 00:45:09,958
Barangay Agulan? In Estrella?

592
00:45:11,084 --> 00:45:12,836
You have no idea the strings I had to pull

593
00:45:12,919 --> 00:45:14,337
to get that information.

594
00:45:15,171 --> 00:45:16,506
Even private investigators

595
00:45:16,589 --> 00:45:19,342
won't be able to get
that exact location, okay?

596
00:45:20,385 --> 00:45:21,553
Estrella...

597
00:45:22,053 --> 00:45:23,471
In the neighboring town.

598
00:45:24,472 --> 00:45:26,057
A one-hour drive.

599
00:45:27,142 --> 00:45:28,560
I know that look.

600
00:45:28,643 --> 00:45:29,644
Ana...

601
00:45:31,896 --> 00:45:33,898
There's no harm in trying.

602
00:45:49,330 --> 00:45:51,916
Really?

603
00:45:52,000 --> 00:45:54,586
Okay. Update me about your life.

604
00:45:55,462 --> 00:45:58,214
Oh, your new boyfriend? Really?

605
00:46:08,975 --> 00:46:11,060
Son, Caloy. Caloy.

606
00:46:20,945 --> 00:46:22,697
Oh!

607
00:46:22,780 --> 00:46:25,366
Wow! I hope I get to go on dates too.

608
00:46:25,450 --> 00:46:27,535
And then what happened?

609
00:46:30,622 --> 00:46:31,789
Taxi!

610
00:46:32,290 --> 00:46:33,458
Taxi!

611
00:46:35,460 --> 00:46:36,711
Get in. Hurry.

612
00:46:38,046 --> 00:46:41,049
Sir, to Santa Monica.
Please drive a bit faster.

613
00:46:52,185 --> 00:46:55,188
I missed you. I missed you so much.

614
00:46:55,897 --> 00:46:59,651
Did you miss Mommy, hmm? Did you...

615
00:47:00,443 --> 00:47:02,695
I miss you, Mommy.

616
00:47:20,547 --> 00:47:21,798
Hey, Ben!

617
00:47:21,881 --> 00:47:23,091
You're on speaker.

618
00:47:23,174 --> 00:47:24,425
I'm driving.

619
00:47:24,509 --> 00:47:25,677
Okay.

620
00:47:26,803 --> 00:47:28,137
Hey, stranger.

621
00:47:28,221 --> 00:47:30,139
Are you on your way home
from the atelier?

622
00:47:30,223 --> 00:47:31,474
<i>No.</i>

623
00:47:31,558 --> 00:47:33,142
<i>Did you go to the atelier?</i>

624
00:47:33,226 --> 00:47:34,477
Yeah.

625
00:47:34,561 --> 00:47:35,728
Um...

626
00:47:35,812 --> 00:47:38,982
They told me
you went to grab coffee with Katrina.

627
00:47:41,192 --> 00:47:43,861
Yes. I'm with Kat.

628
00:47:43,945 --> 00:47:45,321
Hey, Ben!

629
00:47:45,697 --> 00:47:46,781
Hey.

630
00:47:47,448 --> 00:47:49,867
Actually,
she tagged me along

631
00:47:49,951 --> 00:47:51,911
to one of her suppliers.

632
00:47:51,995 --> 00:47:54,080
You know Kat, super clingy.

633
00:47:55,123 --> 00:47:55,957
Sorry, Ben.

634
00:47:56,040 --> 00:47:57,542
It wasn't planned.

635
00:47:57,625 --> 00:48:00,169
We might get back late, Ben.

636
00:48:01,796 --> 00:48:03,047
Oh, really?

637
00:48:04,549 --> 00:48:06,301
Well, that's okay, but...

638
00:48:06,968 --> 00:48:09,220
send me your location on your way home.

639
00:48:09,304 --> 00:48:10,722
Location?

640
00:48:12,098 --> 00:48:13,182
<i>Yeah.</i>

641
00:48:13,891 --> 00:48:15,184
If you're going to be out late,

642
00:48:15,268 --> 00:48:16,769
I want to know where you are.

643
00:48:18,187 --> 00:48:19,230
Yeah, okay.

644
00:48:19,314 --> 00:48:21,733
I'll send it later when I'm on my way.

645
00:48:21,816 --> 00:48:23,109
Um...

646
00:48:23,192 --> 00:48:24,861
Where are you now?

647
00:48:25,987 --> 00:48:28,406
I'm still in the office,
but I'm going home in a bit.

648
00:48:28,489 --> 00:48:30,325
I have a PT session with Beth, remember?

649
00:48:30,408 --> 00:48:31,618
<i>Ah, yeah, yeah. That's right.</i>

650
00:48:31,701 --> 00:48:34,162
Okay. Um...

651
00:48:34,245 --> 00:48:36,497
Uh, h-have a good session.

652
00:48:37,373 --> 00:48:40,126
Okay. Keep safe. I love you.

653
00:48:41,377 --> 00:48:43,046
Love you. Bye!

654
00:48:46,507 --> 00:48:48,176
Share your location?

655
00:48:48,259 --> 00:48:50,553
I'll just come up with something later.

656
00:49:30,176 --> 00:49:33,012
<i> This is my new number.</i>
<i>I got rid of the old one.</i>

657
00:50:00,206 --> 00:50:01,708
Attorney, just relax your shoulder.

658
00:50:01,791 --> 00:50:03,459
- Oh, sorry.
- Good. Okay.

659
00:50:03,543 --> 00:50:05,712
Slowly. Deep breaths.

660
00:50:08,631 --> 00:50:10,466
You're getting stronger, Attorney.

661
00:50:10,550 --> 00:50:12,093
- Very good.
- Yeah.

662
00:50:12,176 --> 00:50:13,177
It feels better.

663
00:50:14,595 --> 00:50:16,597
- Okay.
- Just a little more.

664
00:50:16,973 --> 00:50:18,141
- Okay. Wow.
- Okay.

665
00:50:18,224 --> 00:50:19,892
- Attorney.
- Oh, wow.

666
00:50:20,643 --> 00:50:22,729
- Oh, it's better.
- That's good.

667
00:50:22,812 --> 00:50:24,355
- Wow.
- Okay.

668
00:50:24,439 --> 00:50:25,690
Oh, yay.

669
00:50:25,773 --> 00:50:28,359
By the way, Attorney,
thanks for your help.

670
00:50:28,443 --> 00:50:30,611
I went to the town hall.

671
00:50:30,695 --> 00:50:31,612
Okay.

672
00:50:31,696 --> 00:50:34,615
I need to file some papers,
but they gave me permission

673
00:50:34,699 --> 00:50:36,701
to do freelance work here in Vallente.

674
00:50:36,784 --> 00:50:39,412
Okay.
That's good. Congratulations!

675
00:50:39,495 --> 00:50:40,663
I hope you get more patients.

676
00:50:40,747 --> 00:50:41,664
Let me.

677
00:50:42,373 --> 00:50:45,042
Attorney, that doesn't sound right.

678
00:50:45,126 --> 00:50:47,754
It's like saying,
"I hope more people get sick."

679
00:50:47,837 --> 00:50:50,089
No, of course that's not what I meant.

680
00:50:50,840 --> 00:50:54,427
I just want you
to be successful here, and...

681
00:50:54,510 --> 00:50:57,096
yeah, I hope you help a lot of people.

682
00:50:59,474 --> 00:51:00,558
Wow.

683
00:51:02,477 --> 00:51:04,395
- Thank you.
- Mm.

684
00:51:04,479 --> 00:51:08,983
You know, just the act of drinking water
hurts sometimes.

685
00:51:10,193 --> 00:51:12,945
I'm like an old man.

686
00:51:14,030 --> 00:51:17,116
Oh. Harry made a post.

687
00:51:17,200 --> 00:51:20,620
"How can I be handsome
like you Atty. @BenSantos"

688
00:51:22,622 --> 00:51:26,375
Attorney, you don't have to repost it.
Just give it a like.

689
00:51:26,459 --> 00:51:28,795
That'll make my brother happy.

690
00:51:31,964 --> 00:51:33,216
Where is it?

691
00:51:34,467 --> 00:51:37,845
"Harry: I'm finally in college!"
"Beth: Congrats! Proud of you!"

692
00:51:39,931 --> 00:51:42,016
I bet there's no quiet moment
in your house.

693
00:51:42,934 --> 00:51:44,685
- Yeah--
- It must be fun.

694
00:51:45,311 --> 00:51:46,729
You bet, Attorney.

695
00:51:46,813 --> 00:51:50,233
It's just the three of us,
but there's never a quiet moment.

696
00:51:50,316 --> 00:51:53,903
Especially when Harry's around,
even more so when he was in high school.

697
00:51:54,612 --> 00:51:57,782
I'm just glad we were able
to put him through school.

698
00:52:00,451 --> 00:52:01,953
Attorney, I'll go get changed.

699
00:52:02,036 --> 00:52:03,287
- Okay, go ahead.
- Excuse me.

700
00:52:03,371 --> 00:52:05,039
- You know the way, right?
- Yeah.

701
00:52:39,115 --> 00:52:40,783
Uh, excuse me, mister.

702
00:52:42,368 --> 00:52:44,787
Have you seen Attorney Ben?

703
00:52:44,871 --> 00:52:46,122
No, ma'am.

704
00:52:46,956 --> 00:52:48,374
Are you sure?

705
00:52:48,457 --> 00:52:50,209
His car isn't here.

706
00:52:50,293 --> 00:52:52,795
He always greets me when he arrives.

707
00:52:52,879 --> 00:52:56,090
Isn't he usually here
this day of the week?

708
00:52:56,173 --> 00:52:58,926
Ah, yes. He might show up later.

709
00:53:01,846 --> 00:53:03,514
Okay. Thank you.

710
00:53:10,187 --> 00:53:12,023
Tch.

711
00:53:12,106 --> 00:53:14,108
Jeez, my phone's dead.

712
00:53:15,568 --> 00:53:16,903
That's it. That's the house.

713
00:53:16,986 --> 00:53:18,154
I'm sure that's it!

714
00:53:18,237 --> 00:53:20,072
Ana, I'm not so sure about this.

715
00:53:20,156 --> 00:53:22,074
Hardly anyone lives out here.

716
00:53:25,661 --> 00:53:27,246
Kat, please don't give up.

717
00:53:28,205 --> 00:53:31,375
What if the woman came here
at the time of the call

718
00:53:31,459 --> 00:53:32,752
so it wouldn't be traced to her house?

719
00:53:32,835 --> 00:53:34,754
No, no, no. What if...

720
00:53:34,837 --> 00:53:36,255
I mean, that's the only house out here.

721
00:53:36,339 --> 00:53:39,508
It makes sense that she's here
so she could be hidden.

722
00:53:40,259 --> 00:53:42,678
Ana, I'm not sure about this.

723
00:53:51,062 --> 00:53:52,146
That's her!

724
00:53:52,772 --> 00:53:54,774
That's her! I'm so sure that's her!

725
00:53:54,857 --> 00:53:56,734
Wait. Ana, wait.

726
00:53:56,817 --> 00:53:59,236
- Ana, are you sure about this?
- I'm sure, I'm sure.

727
00:53:59,320 --> 00:54:00,905
Are you sure-- Ana, stop!

728
00:54:51,539 --> 00:54:52,456
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

729
00:54:53,207 --> 00:54:56,210
I'm sorry, but...
I think you dropped this.

730
00:54:56,293 --> 00:54:59,171
<i>Hi! I'm Diane.</i>

731
00:54:59,255 --> 00:55:01,007
Can you give me a ride?

732
00:55:01,382 --> 00:55:02,800
What are you doing?

733
00:55:02,883 --> 00:55:04,552
Is it okay to take a photo of my sprain?

734
00:55:04,635 --> 00:55:08,055
<i>I'm just going to send it</i>
<i>to my friend. It'll be quick.</i>

735
00:55:34,415 --> 00:55:35,583
Ana.

736
00:55:36,876 --> 00:55:39,378
- Ana, are you sure?
- Yes! Yes.

737
00:55:39,462 --> 00:55:41,547
Ana. Ana!

738
00:55:42,923 --> 00:55:44,925
- Ana! Ana.
- Excuse me.

739
00:55:49,013 --> 00:55:50,014
Yes?

740
00:55:50,890 --> 00:55:52,391
How may I help you, ma'am?

741
00:55:54,894 --> 00:55:56,645
Do you own this house?

742
00:55:59,607 --> 00:56:01,358
Yes, I live here.

743
00:56:01,442 --> 00:56:03,110
How may I help you?

744
00:56:04,153 --> 00:56:07,156
I am Benjamin Santos's wife.

745
00:56:10,284 --> 00:56:11,452
Um...

746
00:56:13,162 --> 00:56:14,747
Benjamin...

747
00:56:14,830 --> 00:56:17,333
Come on! I know you know him.

748
00:56:17,416 --> 00:56:19,043
You're his mistress, aren't you?

749
00:56:25,466 --> 00:56:27,218
Ma'am? Mistress?

750
00:56:27,718 --> 00:56:30,221
What? You must be mistaken.

751
00:56:30,304 --> 00:56:32,556
I think you have the wrong house.

752
00:56:32,640 --> 00:56:34,058
No, no.

753
00:56:34,141 --> 00:56:35,935
Someone from here has been calling him.

754
00:56:36,018 --> 00:56:37,353
If you're the only one who lives here,

755
00:56:37,436 --> 00:56:39,021
then you're the one
who's been calling him!

756
00:56:39,105 --> 00:56:41,524
Like I said, you have the wrong house.

757
00:56:42,233 --> 00:56:44,151
No one named Benjamin lives here.

758
00:56:44,860 --> 00:56:47,029
You can't fool me.

759
00:56:52,076 --> 00:56:54,745
- Are you calling my husband?
- No, the village patrol!

760
00:56:54,829 --> 00:56:58,916
I'm calling the village patrol
if you don't stop with your accusations!

761
00:56:58,999 --> 00:57:01,085
You better leave
if you don't want to get arrested.

762
00:57:01,168 --> 00:57:03,462
Ana, I think it's time to go.
Come on.

763
00:57:03,546 --> 00:57:05,172
- I'm calling them.
- You won't fool me.

764
00:57:05,256 --> 00:57:06,674
I'll remember that face!

765
00:57:07,133 --> 00:57:09,135
- Come on. I'm gonna drive.
- Get off me!

766
00:57:45,588 --> 00:57:47,590
- Diane.
- This is our stop. Hold on.

767
00:57:51,552 --> 00:57:53,387
- Here's our fare. Thank you.
- Thanks.

768
00:57:53,470 --> 00:57:55,806
Come on, son.
We're staying with Aunt Beth.

769
00:57:56,557 --> 00:57:57,641
Diane.

770
00:58:19,163 --> 00:58:20,497
<i>Ben, Ana was here.</i>

771
00:58:20,581 --> 00:58:22,708
<i>You're getting paranoid.</i>

772
00:58:22,791 --> 00:58:24,877
I always feel like...

773
00:58:24,960 --> 00:58:27,046
I'm discovering new things

774
00:58:27,129 --> 00:58:28,714
that are bringing me closer to the truth.

775
00:58:28,797 --> 00:58:31,550
We're not leaving, you hear me?
We're not leaving!

776
00:58:31,634 --> 00:58:33,677
<i>Diane, I'm happy now.</i>

777
00:58:33,761 --> 00:58:36,931
<i>You just want to keep up</i>
<i>this fantasy of yours.</i>

778
00:58:37,014 --> 00:58:40,142
Just when you think you're safe,
that's when trouble happens.

779
00:58:40,226 --> 00:58:42,102
Jeez, Attorney.
Don't scare me.

780
00:58:42,186 --> 00:58:44,688

Liar! Liar!

781
00:58:44,772 --> 00:58:46,065
<i> What did you find out?</i>

782
00:58:46,565 --> 00:58:48,400

<i>She's a loyalty tester.</i>

783
00:58:48,484 --> 00:58:51,153

I know a way to make her stop.

784
00:58:54,156 --> 00:58:56,575

